.git/

# Every tree below is listed TWICE, rooted and nested. `**/x` alone does not exclude a root-level
# `x` under the matcher kaniko uses: build 2 carried the Validate stage's full dev venv into
# `COPY . /app` — a 45 MB layer against 544 kB of tracked source — even though `**/.venv/` was
# here, and `uv sync` deleting it in the next layer does not take it back out of that one. The
# mechanism is `**/` expanding to something that needs a path separator before the name, so
# `api/.venv/` matches and `.venv/` does not; the rooted form is what actually holds.
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

.vscode/
.kubecoder/
.claude/
# A live check leaves pid files, logs and its tokens here (see .gitignore). Nothing in the image
# reads them and a token must never ride into a layer.
.run/
